{"kind":"artifact","text":"SKILL.md at exact clean head 1e53a6b49241da3d216938b9cedb1ca3ce730d97 on request/agents-md-cut, succeeding 9aa15307. Companion to the AGENTS.md artifact a11e177c and the notes/retire-dot-artifacts.md artifact at the same head; all three must be co-signed together.\n\nWHAT CHANGED, AND IT IS ONE PARAGRAPH. The succession block in discipline 9 gains the first-artifact case, which it did not previously state: where no live artifact covers the change there is no predecessor to retire and the successor rule cannot choose, so this is a first artifact, and you pick the granularity a reader would cite, a package directory or a document, and keep that string stable, because the next merge in that area must match it. Five insertions and four deletions of reflow around it; git diff --stat reads 9 insertions and 4 deletions for the file, the difference being the rewrapped lines either side. No other rule in the file is touched, added to, or reworded.\n\nWHY THIS FILE. AGENTS.md step 5 states that SKILL.md carries the succession rules in full. That sentence was not quite true: SKILL.md stated the wider-path-wins case and the rename and delete cases, and had no sentence for the case where nothing live covers the change. I read the block before choosing the destination rather than assuming the gap, and the missing case is exactly the one AGENTS.md was carrying alone. Restoring it here makes the pointer honest and keeps AGENTS.md at 116 lines, which is the point of the head this artifact belongs to.\n\nA DEFECT IN THIS FILE THAT I DID NOT FIX AND AM NAMING. The whole succession block, from the sentence beginning \"still live reads succession not recorded\" through the end of the `.` paragraph, sits as continuation text under discipline 9, which is about publishing live activity honestly, and its first line begins mid-sentence with no antecedent. It reads like the surviving half of a bad merge. The rules in it are correct and are the ones people need, so i